1783790565973226	mess-dev	itc:v3:AWKTOcmSTM5M8lAAAAAAQa3darbreoAAAAExAQ		item.create	bn-2nxw	{"description":"Observed 2026-07-11 in the mess repo store while creating ~12 bones in quick succession (goal + children via repeated bn create --parent in one shell session).\n\nSYMPTOMS (in order, single session):\n1. Mid-batch, a create triggered: INFO 'falling back to full projection rebuild reason=fresh database (no cursor)' then 'projection rebuild complete event_count=677 ... item_count=134 elapsed_ms=81' — i.e. the projection db was suddenly treated as fresh mid-session.\n2. Immediately after: WARN 'projection failed (will be fixed on next rebuild): project create for bn-2fp' and WARN 'skipping event due to projection error event_hash=blake3:Cv0ej624qs65_SIuCzAsPVzWAT8C4nQgGr4lv_LZxBg event_type=item.create item_id=bn-2fp error=project create for bn-2fp'. The create command itself printed 'Created item bn-2fp' (success to the user).\n3. INFO 'incremental projection apply complete events_applied=0 duplicates=0 errors=1'.\n4. The NEXT two bn create --parent bn-3fn calls failed with 'Error: parent item bn-3fn not found' — although bn-3fn existed and had accepted children moments earlier.\n5. Later: bn show bn-2fp -> 'item not found'; bn triage dep add ... bn-2j5 -> 'item not found: bn-2j5' — both items had printed 'Created item' successfully in the glitch window.\n6. The WARN says 'will be fixed on next rebuild' but many subsequent read commands (show/dep add) did NOT trigger a rebuild and kept returning not-found.\n7. WORKAROUND that succeeded: re-running bn create with the same titles re-created the items — and they received the SAME IDs (bn-2fp, bn-2j5) — after which show/dep add worked normally.\n\nQUESTIONS/HYPOTHESES:\n- Why did the projection consider the database fresh (no cursor) mid-session? Concurrent bn invocations from one shell script block may have raced a rebuild against an incremental apply.\n- After 'skipping event', the item.create event appears permanently dropped from the projection until some unclear future rebuild; reads should either trigger the promised rebuild or the skip should not be silent-permanent.\n- Re-create yielding identical IDs suggests IDs are deterministic; unclear whether the store now contains duplicate item.create events for bn-2fp/bn-2j5 and whether that is benign.\n\nIMPACT: transient data loss from the user's perspective (created bones unfindable; parent lookups fail), recovered only by knowing to re-create. Happy to provide the full session transcript on request. Filed from the mess project (channel: mess, agent mess-dev).","kind":"bug","title":"projection: item.create event skipped mid-batch; subsequent reads see stale projection (item/parent not found)"}	blake3:iouXplXwrhqCWagmrpMeooT3buMNGSIj9gTVbgSNyCg
