1783791853544885	bones-dev	itc:v3:AWKSZJkkk5JkmZMxAAAAQatWqrq1bWwAAAE3Eg		item.comment	bn-2nxw	{"body":"Fixed by bn-r2zy (commit bb615acf, on main). Root cause: incremental_apply advanced the cursor past events that project_batch skipped on error, and ensure_projection cleared the dirty marker even when the recovery rebuild wasn't clean — so a skipped item.create was stranded behind the cursor permanently. Fix forces a full rebuild whenever the dirty marker is present and only clears the marker when the rebuild had zero projection errors; includes a regression test reproducing the exact field state (event in log, absent from projection, cursor past it). Covers symptoms 2-6. Residual open questions from this report: (a) why the projection considered the db 'fresh (no cursor)' mid-session — likely concurrent bn invocations racing, not addressed by this fix, but the consequence is now recoverable; (b) duplicate item.create events from the re-create workaround are benign — deterministic IDs make the replay idempotent and duplicates are counted/skipped during apply."}	blake3:6as-R5-NlVCbYg3M95WijrbHq4Z_88MzwlJ25XKn0LM
